I would like to add environment variables to `.Renviron` programmatically.  This behavior seems less dangerous than injecting code via `.Rprofile`.  The use case that I'm envisioning is if a JSON for authorization exists, then you can add it to the `.Renviron` so that be loaded for auto-authorization.

For example, google* set of package from @MarkEdmondson1234's work https://github.com/cloudyr/googleComputeEngineR/blob/d62f8989571cfe9cfbeb97250808aee6e29f9cb4/R/options.R#L4have the ability to have a auth file specified (e.g. `GCE_AUTH_FILE`).

If this already exists (including outside `usethis`) I couldn't find it.  I'm envisioning something like:

```r

r_environ_path = function(scope = c("user", "project")) {
  # taken from usethis::edit_r_environ
  path <- usethis:::scoped_path_r(scope, ".Renviron", envvar = "R_ENVIRON_USER")
}

add_variable_r_environ = function(
  scope = c("user", "project"),
  envvar,
  value,
  overwrite = FALSE) {
  
  env = Sys.getenv()
  if (!envvar %in% names(env)) {
    if (!overwrite) {
      stop(envvar, " is already set and overwrite = FALSE. ",
           "If you set these in R, please Restart R.")
    } else {
      warning(envvar, " is already set, we are appending definition to ", 
              ".Renviron, so you may need to tidy .Renviron file")
    }
  }  
  
  # taken from usethis::edit_r_environ
  path <- r_environ_path(scope = scope)
  
  if (!readRenviron(path)) {
    stop("Renviron file is malformed according to base::readRenviron")
  }
  values = readLines(path, warn = FALSE)
  out_value = c(
    paste0("# Added at ", Sys.time(),  " from add_variable_r_environ"),
    paste0(envvar, ' = "', value, '"')
  )
  values = c(values, out_value)
  writeLines(values, path, sep = "\n")
  return(readRenviron(path))
}
```

